# Post-mortem: small-jam (seed 1)

**Incident 00:11–00:27 · up to 62 % below the fault-free twin**

The C0 jam caused 99 % of the delay.
Rerouting C0's parcels to C1 would have saved 71 %.

**837** parcel-min of delay · **23** parcels late · **71 %** recoverable

*How we know: proven by 8 replays of this shift · one version of the day, so no error bars.*

## Summary

From 00:11 sorted throughput fell up to 62 % below the fault-free twin. By 00:37 the incident had cost **837 parcel-minutes** of delay, and 23 parcels were more than 10 min late.
Chute C0 jams (F0) explains 99 % ± 5 % (827 parcel-min).

Best fix: **send chute C0's destination to C1 from the jam on (never undone)** would have recovered 595 parcel-min (71 % of the loss).

How we know: the real shift and its fault-free twin, plus replays with each cause removed (R0–R3); see the replay index at the end.

