## Root causes (system conditions)

Each cause was removed in every combination and the shift replayed (exact Shapley values over 4 subsets). *Alone* = recovered by removing only this cause; *last* = what it adds once every other cause is gone.

| # | Condition | Shapley (parcel-min) | Share | Alone | Last | Needed to explain it? |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | chute C0 jams (F0) | 827 ± 42 | 99 % ± 5 % | 832 | 822 | yes, on its own |

How we know: shares use every replay of the lattice (R0–R3); Alone and Last each come from one replay.

Within noise (share no larger than its band, so not ranked): robot R7 breaks down (F1) (10 ± 42 parcel-min).

Interactions: none beyond the noise; the causes add up independently.

Smallest set of causes whose removal recovers at least 90 % of the recoverable loss (each judged against its own replay noise): {F0}.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Trigger and detection</b> — alarm at 00:19</summary>

## Trigger and detection

Trigger: chute C0 jams at 00:10 (F0).
Detection: a one-sided CUSUM on the per-minute shortfall against the twin (k = 0.5, h = 3 in units of the twin's Poisson noise) alarmed at 00:19; the incident window runs 00:11 to 00:27.

How we know: the trigger is the scenario's earliest fault; detection compares the real run with its fault-free twin.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>Resolution</b> — recovered 14 min after the window opened</summary>

## Resolution

Throughput was back within 5 % of the twin, and held there, 14 min after the window opened.

How we know: throughput is the real run's deliveries per minute compared with its fault-free twin.

</details>

<details>
<summary><b>What would have helped</b> — 4 fixes tested · best 71 %</summary>

## What would have helped

Each fix was applied to the real shift at the time shown and replayed to 00:37. Each fix's gain is the median over the histories of each history's own difference.

| Fix | From | Parcel-min recovered | Share of loss | Cost |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| send chute C0's destination to C1 from the jam on (never undone) | 00:10 | 595 ± 42 | 71 % | sort-plan change |
| release 2 spare robots at the first fault | 00:10 | 143 ± 42 | 17 % | 2 robots |
| allow 8 robots inbound per station (now 6) | 00:10 | 23 ± 42 (within noise) | 3 % | dispatch setting |
| clear failed robots off loading points within 1 min (now 5 min) | 00:11 | 0 ± 42 (within noise) | 0 % | floor procedure |

How we know: each fix was replayed from the time shown (X1–X4).

</details>

