<details>
<summary><b>Method and confidence</b> — how the numbers were made and how far to trust them</summary>

## Method and confidence

- **Generated by** switchyard-analysis 1.0.0 · 8 replays (8 changes × 1 history) · loss scored at 00:37 (window end + 10 min) · **noise band** ± 42 parcel-min
- **Counterfactual replay.** The shift was re-run with each combination of causes removed, resuming from the last 5 min checkpoint before the earliest removed cause, and scored at 00:37 as net parcel-minutes of delay against the fault-free twin (same seed, same parcels). Shapley values are exact over all subsets, in integer arithmetic, so the shares add up exactly to the recovered loss.
- **Noise.** Robot paths diverge after any small change, so every replay ran on 1 history: the real one (no dithered copy diverged: 0 of 3 tried). The headline delay and late count are the real history's; every other value is the median across histories; ± is half their range, widened to at least 5 % of the loss because fewer than 5 histories diverged. *Alone*, *Last* and each fix's gain are the median over the histories of each history's own difference. Two values that differ by less than twice that band are reported as a tie.
- **Detection** uses the twin's Poisson noise as the scale. h = 3 is 3.0 times the largest CUSUM value (1.0) seen in 160 simulated hours of fault-free runs whose robot paths were perturbed.


</details>

